 "text": "Hello there! How's your day treating you? You don't need to speak French to help your daughter. You can read her lessons together, and she'll see a warm adult engaging with the language. She would. Lots of little ones do. And it' also great practice for you. French vocabulary is very similar to Spanish, so you' recognize a lot of words. She' learn fast that you' there to support her, not to act like a tourist. Offer a small reward too, it helps motivation. You could practice reading together, and she'll pick up your accent. There are also songs and games you can find online. You've already won, really. You're showing her that learning a language is fun and accessable.",
